  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "note": "One Phoenix, AZ greenhouse, five configurations, isolating what a movable shade screen, a thermal curtain and a heat pump each change. The shade screen is light-guarded so it will not close when the crop is already short of its daily light target. The curtain declares a 0.1 h-1 closed-gap exchange, which is a user input rather than a sourced value, because screen-gap leakage is UNSOURCED in docs/COMPONENT-PARAMETERS.md. The heat-pump rating points are a labeled hypothetical: only the eligibility floors (COP 1.75 at -15 C and a 0.70 capacity derate) are sourced, so replace all five heat-pump inputs with a catalogued unit before quoting any result.",
